# implement_through_alias - an implement head naming a type alias (a struct's, an enum's, a primitive's, an alias of an alias) implements for the type the alias names: its trait and its own methods are reached through the type and through the alias, by value, through a bound and through a trait object, and the program prints what each call returned.
